Z||000000||dizmon_85GT||10-24-2001||02:19 PM||||MY FM STEREO WILL PLAY IN STEREO ONLY SOME OF THE TIME.  SEVERAL LOCAL RADIO STATIONS BROADCAST IN STEREO, BUT MINE ONLY PICKS THEM UP IN STEREO WHEN IT WANTS TO. BAD CONNECTION, RADIO OR ANTENNA? HELP ME AS IT SOUND SO MUCH BETTER IN STEREO THEN MONO.  IT'S THE ORIGINAL AM/FM CASSETTE PLAYER IN 85 GT.||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||10-24-2001||02:49 PM||||I'd say from the full caps yelling that you're doing, your hearing is shot. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seriously, if the little stereo indicator light is blinking on and off, it's just how you are picking up the stations. Unless you are preserving your car for showroom stock class at car shows, I'd ditch the factory radio and invest in a new head unit. You see, they have these things called compact discs nowadays, hehe. If you like the radio, Pioneer makes great tuners. I'm able ot pick up stations 80 miles away with mine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||10-24-2001||02:54 PM||||Its called drift.  The lock on circuit used to track the station as it varies slightly has changed in value.  The caps change capacitance over time and use.  There also is a 19khz signal transmitted superimposed on everystation that is in stero.  This signal tells the reciever that its a stero signal.  The caps in this circuit are also changing in value over time and use.  This is perfectly normal.....get a new unit.  <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
